  "verbalization": "Isoquercitin 2''-O-Gallate appears to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular targets, primarily DNA polymerase iota. This interaction is supported by multiple evidence paths, each linking the compound to a different intermediate that ultimately targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence suggests that Isoquercitin 2''-O-Gallate may act as a modulator of the DNA polymerase iota pathway, which is known to be involved in chromatin modification and gene regulation. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway, including a structurally distinct compound, implies a potential role in regulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through indirect mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the compound's potential to influence epigenetic processes by targeting a central enzyme in the DNA replication and chromatin remodeling machinery.",
